Subject: Predicting species occupancy over time
Message-ID: <zMtmE8_KQXs.iTbaD6FTAwAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/brms-users/c/zMtmE8_KQXs/m/iTbaD6FTAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I would like to use brms for predicting species occupancy over time in a Bernoulli logistic regression and wondered if there is a way to make it a dynamic model, with presence at the first time step t informing the probability of presence at time t+1, t+2, etc.?

Also, if I have coordinates for each data point, is there a way to make the model spatially explicit?

Thank you!!

From u6e3dd74b422c061b at groups.google.com  Sun Mar  4 16:17:05 2018
From: u6e3dd74b422c061b at groups.google.com (Paul Buerkner)
Date: Sun, 04 Mar 2018 16:17:05 +0000
Subject: Re: [brms-users] Predicting species occupancy over time
Message-ID: <zMtmE8_KQXs.s0LilR3aAgAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <zMtmE8_KQXs.iTbaD6FTAwAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
References: <zMtmE8_KQXs.iTbaD6FTAwAJ@brms-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/brms-users/c/zMtmE8_KQXs/m/s0LilR3aAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

brms supports a few autocorrelation structures (for instance ARMA structures), but they are not supported in a bernoulli model.

You could try fitting splines for the time and spatial correlations. For instance,

y ~ ... + s(time, by = species) + t2(x, z, by = species)

where x and z are the sptial coordinates. The by = species terms implies fitting separate splines for each species.

