You can plot prior distributions for instance via

fit <- brm(..., sample_prior = TRUE)
plot(hypothesis(fit, ...))

You cannot plot the likelihood, but you can plot the posterior-predictive distribution, which is way more informative, via pp_check(fit, ...)

