Hi Paul

This is Chi working with Suo together on this project. Thanks for your quick reply. It is very helpful and we really appreciate it!

Based on the communication above,  we believe a cross-classify multi-membership multilevel model may be the most appropriate model for our data, even we are not exactly sure how to build such a model by brm yet.

If we want to step back to do it in a simpler way, like y ~ imps + (1 + mmc(imps1, imps2) | mm(Publisher1, Publisher2)) you mentioned, my question is do we have a choice to choose the prior for imps1 and imps2? Since we have some reason to believe the coefficient of those covariates should follow a positive distribution, rather than just a normal.

Thanks for your suggestion in advance.
Charles

