I am new to Bayesian multilevel modelling and I'm trying to run some very simple models but I always run into the same warning message:

The model looks as followed:

model1 <- brm(y ~ x1+ x2 + x3 +
(1 | id),
data = data)

summary(model1)

Warning messages:
1: Rows containing NAs were excluded from the model
2: In if (nchar(CXX) > 0) return(TRUE): the condition has length > 1 and only the first element will be used

I don't understand the second warning message. Can someone explain it to me and do I have to be concerned about it?

It seems that the warning message does not come from the brms package itself. (All of my packages are updated).

I very much appreciate your help.

