MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HI Paul,

Many thanks for putting together such a great package.

I was wondering is it possible to build multivariate models with multiple outcomes nested in domains as described here: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3031784/

Such models have been extended to longitudinal models (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4863889/ ), models with levels for treatment vs control etc. This paper has an example with Stan code -

Paper: https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/hbm.23052

Code: https://zenodo.org/record/33432#.Wq403q2cbK  - although that code does not use a true multivariate distribution.

Many thanks,
James

